    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "MiMo dispatch through the existing Llama decoder",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "The registry derives its architecture/config/model records from model-class attributes. Adding MiMoModel therefore creates the MiMoForCausalLM entry through MiMoModel.config_class = MiMoConfig and MiMoConfig.arch_string. Registration and the new classes are complementary: Config.from_directory selects the config, while Model.from_config selects its text component.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_b667d5bae8644f8ba3f6ecf32e2f1d41",
              "call_6b902011e50c414bbb17d791f7d8422c",
              "call_203f91f3039048fe92c63e666da90779",
              "call_b3545801d07748f39d651248f60b35c2",
              "call_df72981899454a42a70a58309d074416"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "MiMoConfig forwards derived_model={\"text\": MiMoModel} into LlamaConfig; MiMoModel delegates construction unchanged to LlamaModel. Existing MistralConfig and Qwen2Config use the same override pattern, with no additional guards or argument preparation omitted by MiMo. Config stores the mapping verbatim; both Model.from_config and compile_model's component-hook iteration accept this dictionary form.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_203f91f3039048fe92c63e666da90779",
              "call_9f5c3e14b0b54f838838d38f1c6f18ab",
              "call_d948162cd7f74716abe50067a941df7e",
              "call_212af8d4a52d44a6aed55f87e2294bb0",
              "call_cc5754aaeb604c469b520d5b57df470f",
              "call_b02489911776484294d100644572ee27",
              "call_df72981899454a42a70a58309d074416",
              "call_1ec449fb27164c1a977df7571a87a2bc"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The inherited decoder constructs model.embed_tokens, 36 model.layers.i blocks, model.norm and lm_head for the reference configurations. Each block uses input_layernorm, separate q_proj/k_proj/v_proj/o_proj attention projections, post_attention_layernorm and gate_proj/up_proj/down_proj MLP projections. prepare_inputs retains the input IDs and invokes the shared attention preparation mechanism; there is no MiMo-specific forward implementation.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_203f91f3039048fe92c63e666da90779",
              "call_9f5c3e14b0b54f838838d38f1c6f18ab",
              "call_d0ad27171eb14676879a34da23c61d28",
              "call_877612bba7a4495688c2cb94ff8bd1bb",
              "call_e5fbe8a85e614ffc97c0a9cb871c8f4e"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "All five inspected XiaomiMiMo configurations\u2014MiMo-7B-Base, MiMo-7B-RL, MiMo-7B-RL-0530, MiMo-7B-RL-Zero and MiMo-7B-SFT\u2014declare the new identifier and agree on hidden width 4096, intermediate width 11008, 36 layers, 32 query heads, eight KV heads, explicit head width 128, SiLU, RMS epsilon 1e-5, theta 640000 and untied embeddings. Thus each fits the inherited dimensional mapping without using the missing-head-width or missing-KV-head defaults.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_e5fbe8a85e614ffc97c0a9cb871c8f4e",
              "call_64c62fc64166484093ec2088a7573974",
              "call_bbe039d6ff8f4fc3b2a11371a6e8303d",
              "call_09253f45d00045119c8ffd2115e90a92",
              "call_3e0611600f1a4238982117ba2db89c53",
              "call_9f5c3e14b0b54f838838d38f1c6f18ab"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Base, RL, RL-Zero and SFT supply a 32768-position limit; RL-0530 supplies 65536 and null rope_scaling. The shared RoPE reader propagates these limits and theta using NEOX style. All five disable sliding-window attention, consistent with LlamaModel not supplying a window. RL and SFT explicitly supply BOS/EOS IDs, whereas Base and RL-Zero omit them and receive Config's None defaults; RL-0530 also supplies them.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_e5fbe8a85e614ffc97c0a9cb871c8f4e",
              "call_64c62fc64166484093ec2088a7573974",
              "call_bbe039d6ff8f4fc3b2a11371a6e8303d",
              "call_09253f45d00045119c8ffd2115e90a92",
              "call_3e0611600f1a4238982117ba2db89c53",
              "call_b3545801d07748f39d651248f60b35c2",
              "call_9f5c3e14b0b54f838838d38f1c6f18ab"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Across all four Base headers, the requested ordinary weights exist: embedding/head [151680,4096], Q/O [4096,4096], K/V [1024,4096], gate/up [11008,4096], down [4096,11008], and norm vectors [4096]. Q/K/V biases have widths 4096/1024/1024. Linear.load_fp16 detects these biases directly, transposes checkpoint matrices, and permits absent biases and weight_scale_inv; O, MLP and head biases and scale tensors are absent. The untied head exists, so the embedding alternate is unnecessary; separate projections exist, so fused-weight fallback is unnecessary.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_abbe7a1183344e05a1e25cdd7ea1377e",
              "call_c140a19fabef4811ad833de7423c8429",
              "call_34504703a94443f9996b5c35d5a7e6f6",
              "call_eef3eb74b02e46f5aeb5026504bbce77",
              "call_9ef27f408b114a2c9787e48e81367711",
              "call_9f5c3e14b0b54f838838d38f1c6f18ab"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "\u201cNo MTP yet\u201d is implemented by omission, not by a runtime flag. The adapter never reads num_nextn_predict_layers and constructs no model.mtp_layers modules. Base and RL-0530 final-shard headers contain 16 such tensors: five norm vectors, input_proj [4096,8192], three MLP matrices and seven attention weight/bias tensors. Those stored tensors are outside the inherited decoder's requested names.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_203f91f3039048fe92c63e666da90779",
              "call_9f5c3e14b0b54f838838d38f1c6f18ab",
              "call_eef3eb74b02e46f5aeb5026504bbce77",
              "call_42de2152b8534ac18572a8d01aa08781"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library metadata calculation reproduced projection dimensions, four query heads per KV head, 39 top-level modules and 435 ordinary tensors. Adding the 16 ignored MTP tensors yields 451, matching the four Base header counts. All matrix dimensions are multiples of Linear's 128-element padding unit. This is scalar metadata validation, not model execution.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_d21232be41f548f68fcb99d0f296b6f9"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [],
    "summary": "Registers MiMoForCausalLM through thin Llama-derived classes, matching the inspected reference configurations and Base tensor layout while deliberately ignoring MTP tensors."
  },
